  "description": "JFET common-source gain stage: Run Off Groove's Fetzer Valve, a JFET in place of the first 12AX7 stage of a Fender amp (runoffgroove.com/fetzervalve.html, Fig. 1, v1.1, © 2004 runoffgroove.com, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0): C1 100n in (ours: the source has none), R3 68k, R1 1M gate to ground, R2 1k5 source with C3 22µ across it, TR1 100k trimmer as the drain load, C2 22n out to a 100k audio Volume (VR1). TR1 is solved to put Q1's drain at 4.5 V, as the drawing says (\"adjust trim for 4.5v at drain\"): the usual way to bias a JFET whose Idss and Vp vary from part to part. A J201, the page's main example.",
