  "notes": {
    "part:TR1": "Run Off Groove: \"adjust trim for 4.5v at drain\". The app solves it to that for the J201 card; set it on the bench for your own JFET.",
    "part:R3": "R3 (68k) and R1 (1M) as the Fetzer Valve's input.",
    "part:C3": "Bypasses R2, so the source sits at AC ground: more gain. Without it the gain falls to about Rd/Rs.",
    "part:C1": "Not in the Fetzer Valve, which takes the guitar straight to the gate: added so the block works after any stage, whatever DC it sits at (the user, 9d3). 100n into R3 + R1 rolls off below about 1.5 Hz."
